[style name="VisualNovelDialogueStyle"]
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/scarecrow BG.2.png" fade="2.0"]

audio music "res://assets/music/VN music.wav"
[i]You walk up to the homely camper. As you approach, the smell of sickly, rotten sweetness hits your nose as you notice a decayed pumpkin sitting on the sidewalk[/i]
audio "res://assets/sfx/Scarecrow Doorbell.wav"
[i]Holding your breath a bit, you ring the doorbell. A few moments pass. And then another few[/i]
[i]You see light streaming from the window. There must be someone inside, and you’re not leaving without candy. A whole minute passes until someone opens the door[/i]

[i]He coughs awkwardly[/i]

SCARECROW: “Sorry ‘bout that kid, didn’t want to get up durin’ the best part of Brewin’ Bad”
SCARECROW: “So, what’re ya here for?”

MC: (I was so distracted comparing him to the rotten pumpkin I almost forgot…)
MC: “Trick or treat!”

[i]The scarecrow stares at you. You stare back. He sniffs. You continue staring. As you’re about to break the silence he finally speaks[/i]

SCARECROW: “Kid, I’ll be honest with you, a guy like me has nothin’ to do on a day like this. I’d usually be out with my youngsters on Halloween, but, y’know, can’t really do that when the ex-wife’s got them for the week”

[i]He laughs for a moment and abruptly returns to a deadpan look[/i]

SCARECROW: “What I’m sayin’ is, I’m eatin’ all the candy in this place. Good luck with the next neighbor though”

MC: (No! I can tell he has the good stuff! I have to convince him)

[signal arg="battle_ui"]

#Battle Start
#Round 1
SCARECROW: “Can ya leave me alone?”
- If your ex-wife knew you gave me candy she’d like you more #3
	set {choice_id} = "A"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	SCARECROW: “That’s wishful thinkin’, let’s be honest”

- I didn’t think you could get any bummier #1
	set {choice_id} = "B"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	join SCARECROW (happy) center
	SCARECROW: “Okay, you got me there”
	join SCARECROW (default) center

- I could be your new kid #2
	set {choice_id} = "C"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	SCARECROW: “CPS would probably have a word with me”

- Look, if I don’t get this candy I’m bashing your pumpkin skull in #4
	set {choice_id} = "D"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	SCARECROW: “I wouldn’t mind all that much”

#Round 2
SCARECROW: “Why’re ya even visiting my place?”
- Someone like you has probably hoarded a ton of candy #4
	set {choice_id} = "A"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “And you’d take away a guy’s only source of happiness?”

-You live in a white van, it’s screaming ‘free candy’ #2
	set {choice_id} = "B"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “Hey, don’t frame me as some sorta serial killer”

-A dad would be inclined to help a kid in need #1
	set {choice_id} = "C"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	join SCARECROW (happy) center
	Scarecrow: “And your need is candy? (Actually ya sound like me)”
	join SCARECROW (default) center

-So I could watch a pathetic old man wallow in his misery #3
	set {choice_id} = "D"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “You got awful taste”

#Round 3
Scarecrow: “I’m probably the worst guy to be talkin’ to right now”
-You might be the least threatening guy on this block, actually #4
	set {choice_id} = "A"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “Death’s honestly more interestin’ than me”

-Traumadumping on a kid is crazy #2
	set {choice_id} = "B"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “Yeah, and who’s the kid still hangin’ ‘round listening to me?”

-Therapy could help you #1
	set {choice_id} = "C"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	join SCARECROW (happy) center
	Scarecrow: “Appreciate the thought but even a therapist’ll lose their mind hearin’ me every week”
	join SCARECROW (default) center

-I agree, the only thing you’re good for is giving candy #3
	set {choice_id} = "D"
	[signal arg="choice_made"]
	Scarecrow: “Guess that’s why she left, huh?” 


# FAIL
SCARECROW: “Look, we both don’t wanna be here. Best if we just part ways—you’ll get better candy from a nicer neighbor and I’ll get to eat mine in peace”

[i]You raise your hand to object but the door slams shut in your face. He gave up on himself faster than you did[/i]

# SUCCESS
SCARECROW: “I appreciate ya makin’ my day even the slightest bit brighter. I haven’t socialized in a bit, ‘n I wasn’t lookin’ forward to, but maybe a bit of change is what I need in life”

[i]He scratches the stubble on his chin and looks into the air[/i]


SCARECROW: “...Y’think she’ll come back to me if I start improvin’ on myself?”

[i]You shift around awkwardly[/i]

MC: “Can I… have my candy now?”

SCARECROW: “Oh yeah yeah, I got you kid”

[i]He tosses his entire bag of candy into your basket[/i]

SCARECROW: “And one more thing”

[i]He raises his now free arm into the air as a crow descends from the sky, perching on him[/i]

SCARECROW: “Thing won’t stop pesterin’ me for attention, but maybe you could be a better owner”

MC: (Is he really shoving things onto me?)


[signal arg="next_house"]